1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:08,600
Tebeje, they will tell you. Tebeje the
drunk. Tebeje the chicken trader.

2
00:00:08,892 --> 00:00:18,071
'Which chicken trader?' 'That drunkard of
Gulele.' 'Oh! Me, Tebeje, I am ruined,' he

3
00:00:18,071 --> 00:00:19,492
said, shaken.

4
00:00:19,808 --> 00:00:25,531
'Gulele is asleep. If I sit under this
eucalyptus and drink, no one will see me,'

5
00:00:25,531 --> 00:00:26,308
he thought.

6
00:00:26,600 --> 00:00:33,047
'Is the woman saved?' he asked tenderly.
One came closer: 'It's a pig you pulled

7
00:00:33,047 --> 00:00:33,450
out.'

8
00:00:33,767 --> 00:00:41,638
'If I slip out, just today, just a little,
just once, just me... what harm could it

9
00:00:41,638 --> 00:00:42,017
do?'

10
00:00:42,308 --> 00:00:47,411
Like a beloved leader they carried him on
their shoulders, passing him along,

11
00:00:47,411 --> 00:00:48,008
cheering.

12
00:00:48,308 --> 00:00:58,601
A great force struck him from behind. A
fox hole caught him in front. His leg

13
00:00:58,601 --> 00:01:01,408
shattered like glass.

14
00:01:01,725 --> 00:01:08,336
'How many legs do I have?' he asked.
Weyzero Tiruneshe replied, 'How many did

15
00:01:08,336 --> 00:01:10,225
you have before, sir?'

16
00:01:10,517 --> 00:01:20,113
Looking at the sky he said, 'For me, drink
means death.' It was night. 'Nights of

17
00:01:20,113 --> 00:01:25,207
such vows pass,' Weyzero Tiruneshe
replied.

